We use the distance formula:  \begin{align*}
\sqrt{(2 - (-4))^2 + ((-6) - 3)^2} &= \sqrt{6^2 + (-9)^2}\\
& = \sqrt{36 + 81}\\
& = \sqrt{117} = \boxed{3\sqrt{13}}.
\end{align*}

We plug in $x = 4$: \begin{align*}
3(4) + 2y &= 12\\
12 + 2y &= 12\\
y &= 0.
\end{align*}

Therefore, $b = \boxed{0}$.
